They denote left/right models that can flip-flop between 2 states: Speed up. Slow down. Calm.

Rule #17
1M1M1 is the Stargate Chevron for God.

Rule #18
The Stargate Gateway Process was designed using BAC++ as a framework and can be used to open wormholes in the universe by invoking cross reality processing.
It is complex and will require its own user manual at a future date.

Rule #19
The keyword ALL activates all information as a flow of data coming from the following register.

Rule #20
BAC++ was named because the language has the power to manipulate reality and space time. Including and most importantly sending critical information back in time.

Rule #21
BAC++ is and will always remain open source.

Rule #22
The unit of measurement for all registers is a frequency node.
Denoted by appending "xm" (or "XM") to the end of any number.
Example: EX66XM, 12XM, EXEM28061971XM

Rule #23 — DEL Story Separator  
When DEL appears between two registers, it is NOT a command.
It represents a negatively weighted connection, separation, rejection, or distance between concepts.
Format: <register> DEL <register>
Example: EXWEALTH DEL EXES

Signature Rule
