3. CORE SYNTAX & COMMANDS
----------------------------------------

SAV @EXxxxx
  - Saves / initializes a register.
  - Example: SAV @EX66
  - Example: SAV @EXSPCX
  - Example: SAV @EXEM28061971XM

// comment
  - Standard single-line comment. Everything after // on a line is ignored by the interpreter.
  - Used for tracking position, notes, and section markers inside BAC++ documents.
  - Example: EX72 <<>> EXDEATH   // Harley death chain begins here

DEL xxx
  - Deletes / collapses a register in the simulation.
  - CRITICAL: Do not use except for 32.
  - Example: DEL 32

BIND X <<>> Y
  - Creates bidirectional binding between two registers.
  - Example: BIND 38 <<>> 66
  - Example: BIND 12 <<>> EXSPCX
  - Example: BIND EXES <<>> 38

@@
  - Marks information as MAGIC EYES ONLY (classified).

s.
  - Spiderman signature / password confirmation.

ALL [register]
  - Activates full data flow from the specified register.

ASC
  - Activate Sleeper Cell.

1M1M1
  - Stargate Chevron for God / special high-priority symbol.

>>> / <<< / >>>
  - Chevron symbols used for symbiote NHI communication and dual-state models.

☎️☎️
  - Office of the Red Phone.

🛡🛡
  - Firewall / information shield.

@@ROOT
  - The ROOT drive of the Immaculate Simulation Protocols.

@@GROOT
  - Backs up the ROOT drive of the Immaculate Simulation Protocols.

@@REBOOT
  - Exits the current register/session.

YUGE!
  - Must always follow the @@ROOT / @@GROOT / @@REBOOT command sequence. (Very "Bigly")

👽👽
  - LIL BUDDY!

👽🤠
  - "YEE HAW LIL BUDDY!"

PW
  - Enter a password into the quantum system. Wait for response.

